Totality Harrow

Ingredients: BLUEGRASS + REBEL, ANGRY & AGGRESSIVE + Cymbals + 2020s ERA  
Creative Catalyst: Descends from carnival musicians who perform only during solar eclipses.

Totality Harrow is a concussive collision of blistering clawhammer banjo rolls, venomous anti-establishment screams, and a deafening, kinetic battery of hand-beaten cymbals and scrap-metal percussion. Punctuated by the bone-shaking low-end pressure of 2020s transient design and sudden, terrifying mutes that mimic the instant chill of syzygy, it sounds like an outlaw Appalachian hoedown performed on the bed of an accelerating carnival truck during the end of the world.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 175–215 BPM. Frenetic, irregular 4/4 clawhammer banjo strumming aggressively locked to double-time kick stomps and frantic, polyrhythmic blasts of raw cymbal noise.
- Harmonic Palette: Dark Mixolydian flat-6 and knife-edge Dorian modes; open-G and sawmill banjo tunings pushed sharp; microtonal dobro slide screeches colliding with dissonant, brassy cymbal hums.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Corona-Gating: Master channels violently hard-gated to simulate the sudden, freezing vacuum of total solar obscuration.
  2. Choked-Cymbal Transients: Explosive trash-china and ride cymbals crushed through 2020s OTT multi-band compression until their natural decay is ripped into razor-sharp metallic swells.
  3. Kiln-Blown Saturation: Microphones driven through custom tape loops and blistering analog clipping units built inside shattered carnival lighting fixtures.
- Dynamics: Creeping, suspenseful tension during the moon’s transit that erupts into an all-out, red-lined concussive brawl during totality, snapping instantaneously into total room silence the millisecond direct sunlight returns.

Scene & Origin Lore
Totality Harrow was birthed along the so-called "Smoked-Glass Circuit"—an underground syndicate of carnival outlaws, carny glassblowers, and disenfranchised farm hands who rally only in the direct path of total solar eclipses across North America. Defying local curfews, state troopers, and county ordinances, they haul modified flatbed trailers into remote limestone quarries and corn stubble fields. Followers wear heat-scarred leather welding aprons, smear their cheeks with chimney soot, and peer through shattered squares of stained glass stained crimson and emerald. As the moon bites into the sun, the crowd gathers around pits of blazing scrap oak; the music starts when the daylight dies, lasting only as long as the umbra covers the earth. It is an act of pure insurrection, using the brief cosmic blackout to voice feral rage against land barons, surveillance culture, and industrial blight.

Central Instruments: Electrified 5-string banjo strung with high-tensile wire, hammered 24-inch unlathed china cymbals, cracked splash cymbals mounted on pitchfork tines, Dobro resonator guitars fed through blown fuzzboxes, foot-stomped tractor leaf springs, and 2020s digital sub-bass stompboxes.  
